[00:03] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Welcome to CleanShot version 5. It\'s been a while, but we wanted to make sure this release was excellent and lived up to the quality you expect from CleanShot. The big new feature in this version is a new screen recording mode. Standard screen recording is'

[00:16] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: "What is Studio Mode?" modal explaining editable projects, zooms, cursor effects.
AUDIO: 'still here and is ideal for quick, everyday recordings. As before, the video is available immediately upon completion of recording and ready to share. There\'s also Studio Mode, new in CleanShot 5, which is the one you\'ll want to'

[00:28] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'use when recording something more important. It\'s ideal for polished social media videos , detailed screencasts, and product demonstrations like the one you \'re watching now. The key advantage of studio mode is that you can'

[00:42] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: CleanShot X editor interface with timeline, zoom controls, and keystroke settings.
AUDIO: 'basically change everything after you finish recording. This allows you to turn mouse clicks and sounds on or off , regardless of whether you remembered to configure them as you wanted when you started recording. I\'m going to record a simple screencast right now to'

[00:57] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: Timeline showing "Zoom 150%" and "Zoom 200%" segments.
AUDIO: 'get into studio mode and show you all the cool things you can do there. Okay, the recording is over and you can see that we\'re now in the new video editor. The first thing you might notice is that, when'

[01:10] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'recording in studio mode, the recording will have zooms automatically applied. CleanShot automatically places zooms on the timeline using a smart algorithm to decide which parts should be shown in detail. These zooms are'

[01:22] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: Zoom level slider at 163%, "Follow Cursor" mode selected, showing a webpage with "Mac mini".
AUDIO: 'fully customizable and easy to adjust to your liking. Click on any of the zoom levels to see its settings. You can change the zoom level, switch from following the cursor to'

[01:35] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: Timeline with multiple zoom segments, demonstrating zoom adjustments.
AUDIO: 'manually placing where the zoom should occur, and update the animation settings to define whether they are smooth or dynamic. You can also click to add a new zoom anywhere on the timeline. You can'

[01:47] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'drag either end of a zoom to extend or reduce it. You can even zoom from one position to another by joining two zooms so that they are connected like that. If you no longer want a'

[01:59] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: Video editor with zoom animation settings (Smooth, Dynamic).
AUDIO: 'zoomed-in view, simply click on it and press delete (backspace). You can also right-click on a zoom to view some of the parameters mentioned or remove all zooms'

[02:12] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'from the timeline at once. In previous versions of CleanShot, you could trim the beginning and end of a recording, but in version 5 you can cut any part you want. Simply select the'

[02:24] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: Timeline with a cut operation indicated by a red line and "⌘B" shortcut.
AUDIO: 'cutting tool and start editing . You can also use keyboard shortcuts for this. You can press B to select the cutting tool and press command B to immediately split at the current head position. There are also many'

[02:37] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: Cursor customization panel with size, style, motion, and click effect options.
AUDIO: 'customization options you can use to make your videos unique. In screen recordings and product demos, the cursor is important, and CleanShot lets you customize your mouse to look and work the way'

[02:50] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'you want. You can change the cursor size or appearance to suit the type of recording you are doing. You can also determine how the mouse should move. The " natural" option slightly cleans up the mouse arcs and'

[03:02] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: Cursor customization showing color picker for ripple animation, with "Pink" selected.
AUDIO: 'trajectories in the video, while "smooth" really smooths everything out. You have more control than ever over clicks, including a subtle effect that makes it look like the mouse is'

[03:15] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'pressing the screen, plus CleanShot\'s classic wave animation, which you can customize with colors and a fill style if you prefer. Finally, you can hide the cursor when it\'s not moving and while'

[03:29] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: Keystrokes settings panel, showing size, style (Dark), position, and "Show only command keys" option.
AUDIO: 'you\'re typing. If you typed something during a screen recording, you can display it using the pressed keys feature . Just like with the mouse, you can change the size of these. You can choose between dark or light mode'

[03:42] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: Audio settings panel with toggles for microphone and system audio.
AUDIO: '. You can choose its position on the screen and decide whether you want to see only the command keys or every key you press. The audio settings are simple and allow you to decide whether to'

[03:55] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'include the microphone and system audio in your final recording. Did you forget to turn on system audio when you started recording? Don\'t worry, you can activate it now after recording. If you recorded your camera during'

[04:09] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: Video editor showing camera overlay on screen recording.
AUDIO: 'screen recording, you can change its size, shape, and position. You can also invert it and make it subtly shrink when you zoom in, which looks really cool. And if you change your mind, you can deactivate it completely. If you'

[04:21] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: '\'ve already used the background feature for screenshots, you\'ll be familiar with how the background for video works. This works especially well when you record a specific window or part of your screen. You can'

[04:34] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'select from different background colors, gradients, or add your own images. You can also adjust the margin around the recording, the intensity of the shadow, and the rounding of the corners. Additionally, you can'

[04:46] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: Motion blur settings with "Medium" selected and "Dynamic" zoom animation.
AUDIO: 'set the aspect ratio that best suits your video. If you\'re going to upload it to YouTube, you\'ll probably want 16 by 9. If you\'re going to upload it to TikTok, 9 by 16 is probably best. And there are, of course, other options'

[04:59] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'for different scenarios. The last customization is motion blur, which comes in the middle by default and looks great, but you can turn it off if you prefer, or even increase it. Now that you\'ve made all'

[05:11] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: "Exporting video..." progress bar.
AUDIO: 'the changes and customized the video perfectly, you\'re ready to export. Press the export button at the top right, select the resolution, the quality, whether you want audio or not, and export it.'

[05:23] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'CleanShot is a fully native Mac application and its export performance is best in its class. When it\'s finished, you\'ll see the video appear on your screen like any other screenshot or recording, and you can'

[05:36] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: "Save As" dialog for saving the project file.
AUDIO: 'save it, upload it, or do whatever you want with it. You can also save the project file to close it and edit it again later . CleanShot has always allowed you to'

[05:48] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: Editing a standard video recording, showing background options and timeline.
AUDIO: 'press space to capture a single window when taking a screenshot, and now you can do the same with screen recordings. By doing this, the video editor will automatically add a background for you. You\'ll also be happy to know that'

[06:02] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'regular screen recordings now have this new video editor. You won\'t have as many customization options, but you retain the ability to add zooms and make cuts anywhere on the timeline. This improves the flexibility'

[06:14] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: Editing a standard video, showing cursor customization options.
AUDIO: 'of your standard recordings, but if you need all the available features, you\'ll still prefer studio mode. It\'s also worth mentioning that this new studio mode is available in both CleanShot'

[06:26] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Basic and CleanShot Pro. We have many ideas for new features in this editor, and this is definitely just the beginning. Before we go, I should mention that there are keyboard shortcuts for almost everything we just'

[06:39] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: CleanShot X settings panel displaying keyboard shortcuts for the Video Editor.
AUDIO: 'showed, and you can see them in the app\'s redesigned settings panel . We\'d love to hear your thoughts on this update in the comments, and if you have any ideas on how we can further improve our video editor, we\'d love to'

[06:52] [scene:talk]
